===== POST /object_set/{project_id}/similarity_search/{object_id}
Returns, in given project, the objects matching the filter and similar to the queried one.
body: {'$ref': '#/components/schemas/ProjectFilters'}
params: [('project_id', 'Internal, numeric id of the project to search in.'), ('object_id', 'Object ID to search similar for.'), ('size', 'Return at maximum this number of object IDs, by default 100.')]
===== POST /object_set/classify_auto_multiple
**Set automatic classification** of a set of objects.

**Returns the number of updated entities.**
body: {'$ref': '#/components/schemas/ClassifyAutoReqMult'}
params: []
===== POST /object_set/classify_auto
**Set automatic classification** of a set of objects.

**Returns the number of updated entities.**
body: {'$ref': '#/components/schemas/ClassifyAutoReq'}
params: []
===== POST /object_set/predict
**Start a prediction** AKA automatic classification for the given object set and options.
body: {'$ref': '#/components/schemas/Body_predict_object_set'}
params: []
===== POST /object_set/{project_id}/revert_to_history
**Revert all objects for the given project**, with the filters, to the target.
body: {'$ref': '#/components/schemas/ProjectFilters'}
params: [('project_id', 'Internal, numeric id of the project.'), ('dry_run', 'If set, then no real write but consequences of the revert will be replied.'), ('target', 'Use null/None for reverting using the last annotation from anyone, or a user id for the last annotation from this user.')]
===== PUT /projects/{project_id}/prediction_settings
**Update the project's prediction settings**, return **NULL upon success.**

🔒 Unlike during full project update above, which needs high permissions, this entry point is accessible
to **project annotators**, as it mirrors the prediction privileges.
body: {}
params: [('project_id', 'Internal, numeric id of the project.'), ('settings', 'The new prediction settings.')]
===== GET /instruments/cnn_networks
Returns the CNN networks (deep feature extractors) which can be used for each instrument,
from the available networks whose name starts with the instrument one.
body: {}
params: [('instrument', 'Only return the CNN networks for this instrument.')]
